		<link href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=32187#p32187"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Contact force dependent friction calculation]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=32187#p32187"><![CDATA[
Going over the PGS paper by Catto, I noticed the main reason for using weight dependent (as opposed to contact force) friction was used to simplify the solver for friction constraints by removing the interdependence between contact and friction. In the case of an iterative solution solver that can probably save quite a bit of time, and general use prioritizes speed over accuracy. But for the case of a direct solver, is the interdependence an obstacle to finding a solution in reasonable time, or is solving still complicated by that interdependence?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9711">Basroil</a> — Tue Nov 19, 2013 7:17 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
